      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T14:34:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ANGLE\u0027s D3D11 backend implements multisampled_render_to_texture by allocating a full MSAA buffer and doing the resolve and discard when a buffer read is needed. I suspect that not using multisampled_render_to_texture and doing it yourself will always be better using ANGLE D3D11 because you get explicit control over when the resolve happens.\n\nUsing multisampled_render_to_texture is likely only going to be a performance improvement on tilers. We support it in D3D11 for compatibility between desktop and mobile on WebGL.",
      "parentUuid": "db34b954_84c0ffc5",
      "revId": "57da581811d59a3b2cd492600b8606752380637a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
